title: Message Discipline
subtitle: Decide what we are actually for.
tags: party_action
new-page: true
view-if: messaging_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; messaging_timer = 1

= Message Discipline

A coalition of college graduates, workers, and minority voters cannot say everything at once. What do we lead with?

- @economic: Kitchen-table economics.
- @democracy: Defense of democracy and the rule of law.
- @identity: Rights and representation.

@economic
subtitle: Wages, health care, prices. Appeals to the working class and moderates.
on-arrival: pop_mod += 0.3; mod_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3; prog_dissent += 1

Simple, concrete, and hard for opponents to caricature.

@democracy
subtitle: Salient when the system is under strain. Costs a little enthusiasm otherwise.
on-arrival: stability += 3; media_trust += 2; pop_mod += 0.4 if maga >= 30; enthusiasm += 2 if maga >= 30; enthusiasm -= 1 if maga < 30

When the rules themselves are at stake, saying so plainly can unite moderates, Republicans-in-exile, and the base.

@identity
subtitle: Energizes the base; risks backlash with swing voters.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 4; prog_dissent -= 4; mod_dissent += 3; pop_mod -= 0.1; far_left += 1

Representation matters. The question is whether we can say it in a way that persuades the people who are not already persuaded.
